Below is the source code

```java
public class Calculator {
	@Inject AsyncExecutor async;

    public int sum(int add1, int add2) {
    	System.out.println("Before Aync call");
    	async.submit(new Callable<Void>() {
			@Override
			public Void call() throws Exception {
				System.out.println("Inside Async Block");
				return null;
			}
		});
        return add1 + add2;
    }
}
```

Below is the test case

```java
@RunWith(MockitoJUnitRunner.class)
public class CalculatorTest {
	@Spy
	private AsyncExecutor async = new AsyncExecutorImpl();
	@InjectMocks
	private Calculator calculator;

	@Test
	public void testSum() throws Exception {
		int result = calculator.sum(1, 2);
		assertEquals(3, result);
	}
}
```

Control is not halting at `System.out.println("Inside Async Block");`  in case of above Junit being debug with a break point inside async block

